You know, you can not only open, but also close the drawbridge by playing
the passtune with a musical instrument.

When the drawbridge comes down, it crushes and kills whoever may be
on the square where the lowered drawbridge is. And when it goes up,
whoever was standing on the lowered drawbridge will drop to the water and
drown if the creature doesn't survive without air. And the closing
drawbridge will also crush anybody who may be standing where the raised
drawbridge is.
Killing monsters by lowering and raising the drawbridge is what I mean by
using the guillotine. A nice technique for getting rid of disenchanters
and liches coming to the opened portcullis, for example.

